# Rust: logging & observability

- Prefer structured logs over stringly logs:
  - Log fields as key/value, not concatenated text.
- Log at the right layer:
  - Libraries should avoid noisy logging by default; return structured errors and let binaries decide what to log.
  - Binaries should log at boundaries (request/job start/end, retries, external calls).
- Avoid logging secrets and PII:
  - Treat tokens, passwords, and personal identifiers as sensitive by default.
- Make logs actionable:
  - Include identifiers needed to correlate events (request id, job id, resource id).
  - Include error chains (root cause) when available.

